k: 449
title: Cook-along
when: weekly saturday
at: 15:30-16:30
min: 25
where: 3 room Mess hall: mess-seat
hold: none
who: dlamini-lukas always, galley 25%, lingers-at-meals 35%, everyone 10%
anim: talk
host: dlamini-lukas
from: dlamini-lukas


== mail
- Cook-along tomorrow at {time} at the galley pass. One simple dish. You stir, you taste, you eat it. Aprons provided.

== ask
- Cook-along this afternoon. We help make dinner. You make it, you eat it.
- Learn a dish at the galley pass later? It's easy.

== here
- Stir, don't splash. Well, splash a little.   #funny
- Taste it. More salt? Less? You decide.
- That's yours. You made that. Look at you.   #warm

== thanks
- At the galley pass, {host} shows you one simple dish. You stir, taste, and walk away with a portion you made yourself.   #warm

== chatter
- Cook-along later. Last week I made soup. Proper soup.
- I can cook three things now. Three!   #funny
- Brennan peeks in at cook-along. Pretends she's not.   #funny
